.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt RPI5-BOOTIMG 8 arm64
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rpi5-bootimg
.Nd rebuild the Raspberry Pi 5 kernel boot image
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl cnqt
.Op Fl b Ar bootdir
.Op Fl r Ar root
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A Raspberry Pi 5 that boots
.Fx
without EFI is started by the VPU firmware, which reads
.Pa config.txt
from the FAT partition of the SD card.
It loads the FreeBSD loader,
.Xr loader.rpiboot 8
.Pq Pa rpiboot.bin ,
as its
.Dq kernel ,
and a small UFS image named by the
.Cm initramfs
line as its initial ramdisk.
The loader has no SD card driver of its own; it loads the
.Fx
kernel and any modules out of that image, and the kernel then mounts its
root file system from the SD card.
.Pp
So the image on the FAT partition has to be rebuilt whenever
.Pa /boot/kernel
or
.Pa /boot/loader.conf
changes.
.Nm
does that: it copies
.Pa /boot/kernel/kernel
and each module named by a
.Va *_load="YES"
line in
.Xr loader.conf 5
into a new image, translates the remaining
.Xr loader.conf 5
variables into
.Ic set
commands for the loader's
.Dq simp
interpreter, takes the root file system from the
.Pa /
entry of
.Xr fstab 5 ,
and installs the result as
.Pa boot.ufs .
The previous image is kept as
.Pa boot.ufs.old .
.Pp
When
.Fx
is installed from base system packages, a
.Xr pkg 8
trigger runs
.Nm
.Fl t
after any package changes files under
.Pa /boot/kernel .
After
.Dl make installkernel
or
.Xr freebsd-update 8 ,
run
.Nm
by hand.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "-b bootdir"
.It Fl b Ar bootdir
Where the FAT partition is mounted, relative to
.Ar root .
The default is
.Pa /boot/efi .
.It Fl c
Also point the
.Cm initramfs
line in
.Pa config.txt
at
.Pa boot.ufs ,
adding one if there is none.
Used once, by the installer, to switch a card from the live system to the
installed one.
.It Fl n
Build the image and show the loader script it would carry, but install
nothing.
.It Fl q
Report only errors and warnings.
.It Fl r Ar root
Operate on the system rooted at
.Ar root
instead of
.Pa / .
.It Fl t
Trigger mode, for
.Xr pkg 8 :
quietly do nothing unless
.Pa config.txt
boots
.Pa rpiboot.bin
and its
.Cm initramfs
line already names
.Pa boot.ufs .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/boot/efi/boot.ufs.old" -compact
.It Pa /boot/efi/config.txt
firmware configuration
.It Pa /boot/efi/boot.ufs
kernel boot image
.It Pa /boot/efi/boot.ufs.old
previous kernel boot image
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
If a new kernel does not boot, mount the FAT partition of the card on
another machine and change the
.Cm initramfs
line of
.Pa config.txt
from
.Pa boot.ufs
to
.Pa boot.ufs.old .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr loader.conf 5 ,
.Xr bsdinstall 8 ,
.Xr loader.rpiboot 8 ,
.Xr loader_simp 8 ,
.Xr makefs 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh BUGS
The image has to start at or above 0x30000000 and end below the top of the
first memory region, which limits it to 244 MiB.
